  "notes": "Two rust-brown steel ribs support the straight deck through slender spandrel columns. Cross-braced steelwork, concrete footings, a lower maintenance walk, four traffic lanes, sidewalks and simple lamps follow exterior photos. The steel span uses the straight plan and published dimensions from the municipal repair inventory. Satellite views differ over the elevated deck; the bridge axis ties to the mapped road ends. The two mapped bridge traces determine the replacement masks. The modeled sidewalks follow the deck edges and transition to the mapped footway at the island landing. Deck elevations, the arch profile and the local approach grading are exterior visual estimates. The west approach compensates for the steep drop in the standard terrain samples.",
